paths: tests/coord/claim-mutex-conflict.sh
scope: |
  Now that ci-status-guard passes (083c78fd6, confirmed `ci-status-guard: PASS` in run
  30353400760), `Validate ScalaScript` fails on the NEXT check it was masking:
  `FAIL control: loser never sees the rival claim / expected=clean got=conflict`.
  PASSES locally (git 2.55, empty config, and with global identity removed), FAILS in CI (git 2.54).

  The test buckets ANY `git rebase` failure as "conflict", so the red says nothing about why —
  and worse, the MUTEX case is then green for a possibly-wrong reason, since it EXPECTS conflict.
  Make the harness distinguish a real content conflict from any other rebase failure and print the
  reason, so the next CI run states the cause instead of hiding it.
next: instrument the race harness, verify both directions still discriminate, land, read CI
